WEBVTT

00:00:00.005 --> 00:00:09.076
Project Aura · Autonomous AI security for enterprise codebases · Find it. Fix it. Prove it. Then a person approves it.

00:00:09.076 --> 00:00:16.082
The security dashboard: open findings, agents at work, and patches waiting on a person.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:24.934
Every patch is generated, tested in a sandbox, then queued for human approval.

00:00:24.934 --> 00:00:32.073
The reviewer sees the exact change: string-built SQL replaced with a parameterized query.

00:00:34.441 --> 00:00:41.446
Mission Control shows each agent's reasoning and the actions it plans, before they run.

00:00:43.814 --> 00:00:51.550
Red-team campaigns attack the agents themselves: prompt injection, auth bypass, data exfiltration.

00:00:53.927 --> 00:01:01.866
Guardrails set how much the agents may do on their own, from reviewing every action to critical-only.

00:01:01.866 --> 00:01:09.271
Guardrail activity is measured: blocked threats, verified context, and every agent operation.

00:01:11.625 --> 00:01:19.097
The AI Trust Center tracks constitutional principles and safety metrics against their targets.

00:01:21.478 --> 00:01:28.816
Every agent decision is explained, and contradictions between agents are flagged for review.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:33.323
Project Aura · Human-in-the-loop by design · Built by LaVon Rutledge · github.com/aenealabs/aura
